  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records repeatedly describe molecular-dynamics tensile deformation of the closely related equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi HEA over multiple temperatures, including partial-dislocation nucleation, stacking-fault accumulation, HCP-like or HCP structures, stress drops at yielding, and thermally enhanced nucleation accompanied by reduced yield stress. Together they make a temperature- and orientation-dependent MD tensile study of an FCC FeNiCrMn crystal, centered on partial-dislocation/stacking-fault plasticity, plausibly reconstructible. However, they do not specifically establish vacancy-cluster nucleation, the selected crystallographic directions, the strain-rate sweep and rate-insensitive yield strength, or the absence of twinning and bulk FCC-to-HCP transformation; indeed, several records instead emphasize TWIP/TRIP and martensitic transformation."
